# Development

The function is plain Python (${{ 'Python 3.13' if '3.13' in values.runtime else 'Python 3.14' }}) with no dependencies to
package. `boto3`, which it uses for DynamoDB, is part of the Lambda runtime.

## Layout

| Path                    | Role                                                              |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/handler.py`        | Lambda entry point (`handler.handler`)                            |
| `src/routes.py`         | Route table: `"<METHOD> <path>"` to handler                       |
| `src/router.py`         | Routing, JSON responses, body parsing, error handling             |
{%- if values.enableCRUD %}
| `src/items/handlers.py` | Handlers of the `/items` endpoints                                |
| `src/items/store.py`    | Items in the DynamoDB table named by `ITEMS_TABLE`                |
{%- endif %}
| `tests/`                | Unit tests (pytest), no AWS access needed                         |
| `scripts/package.sh`    | Writes `build/lambda.zip`                                         |
| `requirements-dev.txt`  | pytest and ruff, the only tools to install                        |

## Run the checks

```bash
python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
ruff check .
pytest
```

## Build the deployment package

```bash
bash scripts/package.sh
```

This writes `build/lambda.zip`, the file `infra/` deploys. The pipeline does
the same through `.github/actions/build-lambda`.

## Implement an endpoint

API Gateway sends every request to the function with the method in
`event["httpMethod"]` and the path template in `event["resource"]` (for
example `/users/{id}`; the value of `{id}` is in
`event["pathParameters"]["id"]`). `src/routes.py` maps
`"<METHOD> <path template>"` to a handler.

An endpoint requested when the repository was created starts as a stub that
answers `501`. Replace the stub with a handler:

```python
from router import json_response, parse_object


def create_user(event):
    user = parse_object(event)
    return json_response(201, user)


ROUTES = {
    # ...
    "POST /users": create_user,
}
```

Raise `HttpError(status, message)` from `router.py` to answer with an error
status. Any other exception is logged and answered with `500`.

A third-party package has to be installed into `src/` before packaging
(`pip install --target src <package>`), because the archive is the content of
that directory.

To add an endpoint that was not requested at creation, add it to `endpoints`
in `infra/terraform.tfvars.json` as well, so that API Gateway routes it; see
[Operations](operations.md#change-the-configuration).
